# Installed to /etc/sudoers.d/klipper-updater (mode 0440) by install.sh, only if
# you accept the prompt. %USER% is substituted there.
#
# Not needed for the normal path: the agent stops and starts klipper through
# Moonraker's machine.services API, which is already privileged and gated by
# ~/printer_data/moonraker.asvc.
#
# This exists for the case that actually hurts - Moonraker dying between the stop
# and the start. The API is then unreachable, and without this the agent cannot
# put klipper back, leaving the printer dead until someone notices and SSHes in.
# It is also what the unit's ExecStopPost safety net uses.
#
# Deliberately narrow: three exact commands for one unit, no wildcards.
%USER% ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /bin/systemctl start klipper
%USER% ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /bin/systemctl stop klipper
%USER% ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /bin/systemctl is-active klipper
